  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1253 PM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nAlthough the monsoon plume will stay over the region this week, the \nquality of the moisture will be less. Likewise, showers and storms \nwill be possible over the region, but there will be less activity \nTuesday through the Thursday time period. Overall, expect scattered \nstorms in the mtns, and isolated activity over the plains. \n\nFrom Friday into the weekend, Deterministic guidance shows moisture \nincreasing through the column during this period. and showers and \nstorms should become more prevalent over the region during this time \nperiod. This same overall pattern is indicated by the statistical \nguidance. Warmest temps should occur late in the week. 100s may come \nback to parts of the far east plains Friday and Saturday. A bit of a \ncooling pattern possible by early next week, but there is \ndisagreement in the guidance about this outcome. \n\nChecking the fire weather parameters during this forecast period, we \nmay see some spotty conditions on Thursday across a small part of \nthe region.",
